            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of postoperative care of a patient having undergone a post-traumatic amputation is to prevent complications and ensure the optimal healing of the amputated limb. The team is especially attentive to pain and supports the patient in their acceptance process.</AbstractText>
